History:
--------

V1.0 / 05-26-94 - Started for internal use.

V1.1 / 06-02-94 - Use this version only with the new version 3.15 or higher!
                  Removed the [V]ersion command because the 2.1 and 3.x are
                  different and the 3.x makes problems.
                  Autodetect Tempest Version included. Now it breaks when you 
                  try to run this Tool below 3.15. Language detect included
                  (default is english, included!) and others can add to your
                  BBS:TEXT/"LANGUAGE"/ directory. Just create them.

V1.2 / 06-08-94 - DISPLAYS ALL ARCHIVING ACTIONS BY LHA!!! Thanks to AMTRAC
                  for adding his routine! Added CLS before leaving the Tool
                  and displaying the About Banner.
                  Seems that some Sysops had problems with the subdir when
                  adding the Files to the archive, removed. Now the files are
                  added simply to an archive without any subdir ("UPDATE!/").
                  Made RETURN to default [Yes], while the prompt

                  "Start Download `Temp_??.lha` [Y/n]:

                  is displayed. (Thanks to CHAD KOVAC for the Ideas)

                  Included a new Textfile ("Text-UpdateTool") that is located
                  in the BBS:TEXT/"LANGUAGE"/ directory. It contains the Rulez
                  for BETA-Testers and is added to the archive if found. If its
                  not found, nothing is added.

                  When downloading an archive it is added to this archive and
                  is called "BetaTester.README!".

                  This gives you the choice to add special BETA-Tester-Rulez
                  for your Board and your Tools. Normaly the default Rulez
                  for Tempest has to be in this Textfile. They will done soon
                  by Michael Bockert. :-)
                  Be sure to have an textfile "Text-UpdateTool" for each
                  language in your TEXT:"language"/ directory!      ~~~~

V1.3 / 06-19-94 - This Version didn't need a DOORS: assignment anymore, because
                  it gets the path of your "DOORS" directory direct from Tempest.
                  (PATH 6).

                  Fixed the output, when the comment has more than 22 chars
                  (will be cut). (Thanks to Chad Kovac for finding the Bug) 
                  
                  The User with Slotnumber '1' (you??? *:-) ) has the abilitiy 
                  to add a Filenote/Filecomment to all Files that are listed 
                  with this Tool...and this Command (F) is added to the 
                  "Updater Menu". (only 22 Characters are displayed)
                  
                  Important: If you are NOT useing "English" Language/Locale at
                             your Computer/System this Tool makes troubles when
                             displaying the DATE/WEEKDAY and "Flagged"-Status!

                  Now the Stats are displayed when leaving the Util. (It creates
                  a file in the DOORS: called "UPDATE!.data".)
                                                                               
